{"clock":31,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"24057e069f00a322244d11bd81dd0c837a630cdc","forge_id":"5997467417","number":"40","url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db/issues/40"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"24057e069f00a322244d11bd81dd0c837a630cdc","field":"title","value":"[SPECS](Dataset) Keep specimen numbers (N) stable across deliveries"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"24057e069f00a322244d11bd81dd0c837a630cdc","field":"body","value":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** Once a test has a number (`N`) in a delivered version of the database, it keeps that number. New tests take new numbers, and existing tests and their files are never renumbered.\n- **Why:** The 22/10/2026 delivery (#37) renumbered the 10 EPFL tests from 189–198 to 227–236 and renamed all their files, although the photos and F-d curves themselves did not change.\n- **User impact:** Links, citations and downloads that name a test number now point to a different test.\n- **Decision needed:** How EESD numbers new tests from now on (options below).\n\n---\n\n### What users experience\n\nThe website addresses each test by its number: `/database?specimen=189`. Before 22/10/2026 that link opened **SW0.1** (Inzunza Araya et al., 2026). Since the update it opens **UMW1** (Churilov \u0026 Dumova-Jovanoska, 2013), with no warning. The same applies to:\n\n- a paper, report or email that cites \"test 189\";\n- a CSV or zip downloaded from the previous version, whose files (`fd_curve_0189.csv`, `fig_setup_0189.jpg`, …) now belong to a different test.\n\n### Why it matters\n\n`N` is the only key that ties together a database row, its curve and photo files, and its page on the website. If `N` changes, everything that refers to the test has to change with it. Anything outside our control, such as bookmarks, citations and downloaded copies, breaks without anyone noticing.\n\nIn this delivery the 10 EPFL tests' photos and F-d curves are byte-for-byte identical to the previous version. Only their numbers, and therefore their file names, changed.\n\n### What we propose\n\nA numbering rule for the dataset, written into its `readme.txt`:\n\n1. A number given to a test in a delivered version is never changed or reused.\n2. A test removed from the database leaves its number unused (\"retired\").\n3. If a renumbering ever becomes unavoidable, the delivery includes an old N → new N table, so we can redirect old links.\n\n### Decision needed\n\nI assume the 37 new tests were inserted at 189–226 to keep the Pavia dataset (Morandi et al.) in one contiguous block. Which rule do you prefer for new tests?\n\n- **A. Append only:** every new test takes the next free number (237, 238, …), whatever its source. This is the simplest option. The table is no longer grouped by source, but sorting or filtering by Reference or Institution restores the grouping.\n- **B. Reserved ranges per source:** for example, the Pavia dataset keeps 1–999 and EPFL campaigns start at 1001. This mirrors Pavia's own numbering, and neither block can push the other.\n- **C. Separate source number:** `N` stays a stable internal ID (as in A), and a new column holds the test's number in its original dataset.\n\n### Done when\n\n- [ ] EESD picks A, B or C.\n- [ ] The rule is stated in the dataset `readme.txt` (GENERAL DESCRIPTION).\n- [ ] The next delivery follows it: every N present in the previous version still refers to the same test.\n\n### Technical notes\n\n- Release 0.1.0 shipped the old numbering. Specimen links shared since then for 189–198 now resolve to other tests.\n- Renamed files in this delivery:\n  - `02_fd_curve/fd_curve_0189–0198.csv`\n  - the envelope and bilinear curves\n  - `fig_setup`, `fig_failmode`, `fig_mat` and `fig_cracks` `_0189–0198.jpg`\n- The photos are stored in git-lfs. A renumbering forces every file to be renamed, and when content changes as well, re-uploaded.\n"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"24057e069f00a322244d11bd81dd0c837a630cdc","field":"status","value":"open"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"24057e069f00a322244d11bd81dd0c837a630cdc","field":"labels","value":""}}]}